🚽 draw.brainrot — every rl_draw_* call in the game lives here.
🚽
🚽 M0 renders in primitives. Sprite atlases need rl_draw_texture_rec
🚽 upstream (DESIGN.md B2), and one PNG per animation frame would mean six
🚽 texture handles for a run cycle alone. Rectangles ship a playable game
🚽 with no upstream blockers, which is the whole point of M0.
🚽
🚽 Numeric HUD text arrived upstream as rl_draw_text_int /
🚽 rl_measure_text_int (DESIGN.md B1, Brainrotlang/brainrot#292), so the
🚽 score, level and final score are drawn rather than printed to the
🚽 console. See DESIGN.md section 10.3.
🚽
🚽 Requires `#cooked <raylib>` earlier in the including file.

skibidi draw_begin() {
    rl_begin_drawing();
}

skibidi draw_end() {
    rl_end_drawing();
}

🚽 `drain` 0 is the normal per-level sky; 1 lerps it toward a dead grey-black.
🚽 The Combinasion reveal (12.6.1) ramps it: the saturation draining out of the
🚽 world is the cue that the joke game is over. Grey-lerp, not a true
🚽 desaturation -- it stays inside this one call with no new colour maths.
skibidi draw_sky(rizz lvl, chad drain) {
    chad d = clampf(drain, 0.0, 1.0);
    chad r = lerpf(sky_r(lvl), 6.0, d);
    chad g = lerpf(sky_g(lvl), 5.0, d);
    chad b = lerpf(sky_b(lvl), 8.0, d);
    rl_clear_background(r, g, b, 255);
}

skibidi draw_ground() {
    chad g = t_ground_y();
    rl_draw_rectangle(0, g, t_screen_w(), t_screen_h() - g, 34, 28, 24, 255);
    rl_draw_rectangle(0, g, t_screen_w(), 6, 58, 48, 38, 255);
}

🚽 --- sprite loading ---
🚽 One loader per atlas, each returning a handle or -1. Hardcoding the paths
🚽 here rather than passing them in keeps every rl_* call inside this file,
🚽 which is the rule that lets the headless harness swap the whole layer out.
🚽 ONE loader, taking the path.
🚽
🚽 There were fourteen of these, identical but for a string literal, because
🚽 a user-defined function could not take a `rant` -- "String parameters are
🚽 not supported". Landed upstream as part of
🚽 [brainrot#311](https://github.com/Brainrotlang/brainrot/issues/311), so
🚽 the workaround is gone.
🚽
🚽 A missing file still returns -1 and every consumer already handles that,
🚽 so cloning without assets still gives a game.
rizz draw_load(rant path) { bussin rl_load_texture(path); }

skibidi draw_unload(rizz tex) {
    edgy (tex >= 0) { rl_unload_texture(tex); }
}

🚽 Tung himself.
🚽
🚽 `tex` is an atlas handle and `frame` an index into it. A negative handle
🚽 means the art is missing, and the game falls back to the M0 rectangle
🚽 rather than drawing nothing -- someone who clones this without the assets
🚽 should get a playable game, not an invisible player.
🚽
🚽 The sprite is wider than the collision box, so it is drawn offset by the
🚽 torso anchor. Its bottom row is the contact row, so y needs no offset at
🚽 all: the feet land exactly where the physics puts them.
🚽 `face` is +1 right (the art's native direction) or -1 left. Tung only ever
🚽 faces left in the Combinasion fight, where he can walk backwards across the
🚽 arena; every other mode passes +1 and draws unmirrored as before. A left
🚽 face flips the source width negative and mirrors the anchor column, same as
🚽 U Din Din.
skibidi draw_player(chad x, chad y, rizz tex, rizz frame, rizz face) {
    edgy (tex < 0) {
        rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, t_player_w(), t_player_h(), 196, 148, 92, 255);
        rl_draw_rectangle(x + 8.0, y + 18.0, 10.0, 10.0, 30, 22, 16, 255);
        rl_draw_rectangle(x + 30.0, y + 18.0, 10.0, 10.0, 30, 22, 16, 255);
        rl_draw_rectangle(x + 12.0, y + 46.0, 24.0, 6.0, 30, 22, 16, 255);
    }
    amogus {
        chad sw   = t_sprite_w();
        chad anc  = t_sprite_anchor();
        chad srcw = sw;
        edgy (face < 0) {
            srcw = 0.0 - sw;
            anc  = sw - anc;
        }
        rl_draw_texture_rec(tex, frame * sw, 0.0, srcw, t_sprite_h(),
                            x + t_player_w() / 2.0 - anc, y,
                            255, 255, 255, 255);
    }
}

🚽 The bat hitbox, as a rectangle.
🚽
🚽 Only drawn when the sprite atlas is missing. With the art loaded the bat
🚽 is part of the swing frames, and the drawn bat is about 18px shorter than
🚽 this box -- so the reach is slightly more generous than it looks. See
🚽 DESIGN.md 10.1.
skibidi draw_bat(chad x, chad y, rizz tex) {
    edgy (tex < 0) {
        rl_draw_rectangle(x + t_hitbox_dx(), y + t_hitbox_dy(),
                          t_hitbox_w(), t_hitbox_h(), 240, 220, 120, 255);
    }
}

🚽 An obstacle or an enemy. Each kind has its own atlas handle and its own
🚽 frame width and anchor, printed by tools/process_sprites.py -- the art is
🚽 not the same width as the collision box, so the draw offsets by the
🚽 anchor rather than using the entity's x.
🚽
🚽 A negative handle falls back to the M0 rectangle, per kind, so a partial
🚽 set of assets degrades one entity at a time instead of all at once.
skibidi draw_ent(chad x, chad y, chad w, chad h, rizz kind,
                 rizz tex_pat, rizz tex_crate, rizz tex_post, rizz tex_vaca,
                 rizz frame) {
    🚽 Vaca Saturno -- the hopping enemy. Two frames, mirrored like Patapim
    🚽 (faces right, charges left). Drawn at the hopped y from ent_scroll.
    edgy (kind == t_kind_vaca()) {
        edgy (tex_vaca >= 0) {
            chad vw = t_vaca_w();
            rl_draw_texture_rec(tex_vaca, frame * vw, 0.0, 0.0 - vw, t_vaca_h(),
                                x + w / 2.0 - t_vaca_anchor(), y,
                                255, 255, 255, 255);
        }
        amogus {
            🚽 A green orb with a cow face, for a missing atlas.
            rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, h, 150, 182, 150, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + w * 0.62, y + 8.0, 14.0, 12.0,
                              240, 240, 240, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + w * 0.66, y + 11.0, 6.0, 6.0, 20, 20, 20, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + 10.0, y + h - 14.0, 10.0, 14.0, 84, 62, 50, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + w - 22.0, y + h - 14.0, 10.0, 14.0,
                              84, 62, 50, 255);
        }
        bussin;
    }
    edgy (kind == t_kind_patapim()) {
        edgy (tex_pat >= 0) {
            🚽 NEGATIVE source width, which mirrors the frame.
            🚽
            🚽 Every sprite is authored facing right, because that is the
            🚽 cheaper half: rl_draw_texture_rec flips on the sign of the
            🚽 source rectangle, so one direction is free. Tung runs right
            🚽 and needs no flip. Patapim charges LEFT at the player, so
            🚽 without this it runs backwards -- tail first, at the thing
            🚽 it is supposed to be attacking.
            chad pw = t_patapim_w();
            rl_draw_texture_rec(tex_pat, frame * pw, 0.0, 0.0 - pw,
                                t_patapim_h(),
                                x + w / 2.0 - t_patapim_anchor(), y,
                                255, 255, 255, 255);
        }
        amogus {
            rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, h, 150, 80, 44, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + 10.0, y + 16.0, 12.0, 12.0, 240, 240, 240, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + 40.0, y + 16.0, 12.0, 12.0, 240, 240, 240, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + 14.0, y + 42.0, 36.0, 8.0, 40, 20, 12, 255);
        }
    }
    amogus {
        edgy (kind == t_kind_post()) {
            edgy (tex_post >= 0) {
                rl_draw_texture_rec(tex_post, 0.0, 0.0, 21.0, 96.0,
                                    x + w / 2.0 - 10.0, y, 255, 255, 255, 255);
            }
            amogus {
                rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, h, 120, 110, 96, 255);
                rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, 8.0, 150, 138, 120, 255);
            }
        }
        amogus {
            edgy (tex_crate >= 0) {
                rl_draw_texture_rec(tex_crate, 0.0, 0.0, 46.0, 48.0,
                                    x + w / 2.0 - 22.0, y, 255, 255, 255, 255);
            }
            amogus {
                rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, h, 96, 92, 100, 255);
                rl_draw_rectangle(x + 4.0, y + 4.0, w - 8.0, h - 8.0, 76, 72, 80, 255);
            }
        }
    }
}

🚽 One parallax layer, tiled across the screen and scrolled at a fraction
🚽 of the world's speed.
🚽
🚽 Each layer is authored at its own width and repeated, rather than being
🚽 one screen-wide image: the apparent HEIGHT of a layer is a composition
🚽 decision, and how many times it repeats to fill 1280px is not. Scaling
🚽 them to the screen width instead produced a foliage band 472px tall
🚽 against a 96px character, which buried the entire scene.
🚽
🚽 `rate` below 1.0 makes the layer lag the ground, which is the parallax.
skibidi draw_layer(rizz tex, chad dist, chad rate, chad lw, chad lh,
                   chad bottom) {
    edgy (tex >= 0) {
        chad shift = dist * rate;
        rizz whole = shift / lw;
        chad off = shift - whole * lw;
        chad y = bottom - lh;
        chad x = 0.0 - off;
        goon (x < t_screen_w()) {
            rl_draw_texture_rec(tex, 0.0, 0.0, lw, lh, x, y, 255, 255, 255, 255);
            x = x + lw;
        }
    }
}

🚽 The four layers, back to front. Rates are the design's: distant hills
🚽 barely move, foliage at the player's feet moves with the ground.
skibidi draw_background(rizz far, rizz mid, rizz near, rizz fore, chad dist) {
    chad g = t_ground_y();
    draw_layer(far,  dist, t_bg_far_rate(),  t_bg_far_w(),  t_bg_far_h(),  g);
    draw_layer(mid,  dist, t_bg_mid_rate(),  t_bg_mid_w(),  t_bg_mid_h(),  g);
    draw_layer(near, dist, t_bg_near_rate(), t_bg_near_w(), t_bg_near_h(), g);
    draw_layer(fore, dist, t_bg_fore_rate(), t_bg_fore_w(), t_bg_fore_h(),
               g + t_bg_fore_drop());
}

skibidi draw_hearts(rizz hearts) {
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < hearts; i = i + 1) {
        rl_draw_rectangle(20 + i * 28, 20, 20, 20, 220, 60, 60, 255);
    }
}

🚽 Eight segments, one per level, matching speed_to_lvl's range.
skibidi draw_speedbar(rizz lvl) {
    rl_draw_text("SPEED", 1064, 18, 20, 220, 220, 220, 255);
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < 9; i = i + 1) {
        edgy (i < lvl) {
            rl_draw_rectangle(1136 + i * 16, 18, 12, 20, 240, 150, 40, 255);
        }
        amogus {
            rl_draw_rectangle(1136 + i * 16, 18, 12, 20, 60, 56, 52, 255);
        }
    }
}

🚽 Score is zero-padded to six columns so the number keeps a fixed width
🚽 as it grows -- a HUD that reflows every time you cross a power of ten is
🚽 the thing `pad` exists to prevent.
skibidi draw_hud(rizz score, rizz lvl) {
    rl_draw_text_int("SCORE ", score, 6, 20, 52, 20, 220, 200, 120, 255);
    rl_draw_text_int("LVL ", lvl, 0, 1064, 46, 20, 220, 220, 220, 255);
}

🚽 The title beat: TUNG... TUNG... TUNG... SAHUR, one word at a time.
skibidi draw_title(chad t) {
    rizz cx = t_screen_w() / 2;

    edgy (t > 0.0) {
        rizz w1 = rl_measure_text("TUNG...", 64);
        rl_draw_text("TUNG...", cx - w1 / 2, 150, 64, 200, 170, 120, 255);
    }
    edgy (t > 0.5) {
        rizz w2 = rl_measure_text("TUNG...", 64);
        rl_draw_text("TUNG...", cx - w2 / 2, 220, 64, 210, 180, 130, 255);
    }
    edgy (t > 1.0) {
        rizz w3 = rl_measure_text("TUNG...", 64);
        rl_draw_text("TUNG...", cx - w3 / 2, 290, 64, 220, 190, 140, 255);
    }
    edgy (t > 1.5) {
        rizz w4 = rl_measure_text("SAHUR", 96);
        rl_draw_text("SAHUR", cx - w4 / 2, 360, 96, 245, 200, 90, 255);
    }
    edgy (t > 2.2) {
        rizz w5 = rl_measure_text("SPACE to jump, X to TUNG, ESC to quit", 24);
        rl_draw_text("SPACE to jump, X to TUNG, ESC to quit",
                     cx - w5 / 2, 480, 24, 190, 190, 190, 255);
        rizz w6 = rl_measure_text("ENTER to start playing", 28);
        rl_draw_text("ENTER to start playing",
                     cx - w6 / 2, 516, 28, 245, 200, 90, 255);
    }
}

🚽 The seed is on screen because a run is reproducible from it: a bug
🚽 report is a seed and a frame number, and asking someone to go read their
🚽 terminal for it never worked.
skibidi draw_gameover(rizz score, rizz seed) {
    rizz cx = t_screen_w() / 2;
    rl_draw_rectangle(0, 232, t_screen_w(), 216, 0, 0, 0, 190);

    rizz w1 = rl_measure_text("GAME OVER", 80);
    rl_draw_text("GAME OVER", cx - w1 / 2, 258, 80, 230, 70, 60, 255);

    rizz w2 = rl_measure_text_int("SCORE ", score, 0, 36);
    rl_draw_text_int("SCORE ", score, 0, cx - w2 / 2, 350, 36,
                     245, 200, 90, 255);

    rizz w3 = rl_measure_text_int("seed ", seed, 0, 18);
    rl_draw_text_int("seed ", seed, 0, cx - w3 / 2, 396, 18,
                     140, 140, 140, 255);

    rizz w4 = rl_measure_text("ENTER to play again", 28);
    rl_draw_text("ENTER to play again", cx - w4 / 2, 420, 28,
                 245, 200, 90, 255);
}

🚽 The reveal's name card (12.6.1): only when his full silhouette is in, and
🚽 the prog track detonates with it. No subtitle -- the sprite has already
🚽 said everything.
skibidi draw_namecard() {
    rizz cx = t_screen_w() / 2;
    rizz w1 = rl_measure_text("LA GRANDE", 88);
    rl_draw_text("LA GRANDE", cx - w1 / 2, 120, 88, 214, 64, 64, 255);
    rizz w2 = rl_measure_text("COMBINASION", 88);
    rl_draw_text("COMBINASION", cx - w2 / 2, 210, 88, 214, 64, 64, 255);
}

🚽 Beating the developer ends the run in a win, not a game over (12.6.11).
skibidi draw_win(rizz score, rizz seed) {
    rizz cx = t_screen_w() / 2;
    rl_draw_rectangle(0, 200, t_screen_w(), 280, 0, 0, 0, 200);

    rizz w1 = rl_measure_text("YOU BEAT THE DEVELOPER", 64);
    rl_draw_text("YOU BEAT THE DEVELOPER", cx - w1 / 2, 226, 64,
                 245, 200, 90, 255);

    rizz w2 = rl_measure_text("SAHUR SAVED", 44);
    rl_draw_text("SAHUR SAVED", cx - w2 / 2, 306, 44, 210, 180, 130, 255);

    rizz w3 = rl_measure_text_int("SCORE ", score, 0, 36);
    rl_draw_text_int("SCORE ", score, 0, cx - w3 / 2, 368, 36,
                     245, 200, 90, 255);

    rizz w4 = rl_measure_text("ENTER to play again", 28);
    rl_draw_text("ENTER to play again", cx - w4 / 2, 424, 28,
                 245, 200, 90, 255);
}

🚽 --- bosses ---------------------------------------------------------------
🚽
🚽 Primitives, deliberately. There is no shark or crocodile art yet, and M0
🚽 proved the game reads fine in rectangles -- so the fight ships playable
🚽 and the atlases drop in later behind the same `tex >= 0` fallback every
🚽 other draw here already uses. Nothing in the simulation knows or cares.

🚽 La Grande Combinasion (12.6). He teleports, so most states draw nothing
🚽 (OUT) or only a ground marker (TELL); once materialised he is a 5-frame
🚽 windup->swing strip, bat-low (0) to bat-overhead (4), faced by dir. The
🚽 marker is truthful -- he lands exactly on it -- which is what keeps the
🚽 teleport fair (12.6.6).
skibidi draw_combinasion(chad x, chad y, chad w, chad h, rizz state, rizz dir,
                         chad dest_x, chad anim, rizz tex) {
    edgy (state == t_cs_out()) { bussin; }   🚽 vanished: no body

    edgy (state == t_cs_tell()) {
        🚽 A faint column where he will appear plus a bright ground bar --
        🚽 read "here, now" without a number.
        rl_draw_rectangle(dest_x, t_ground_y() - t_combi_h(),
                          t_combi_w(), t_combi_h(), 210, 50, 70, 45);
        rl_draw_rectangle(dest_x - 6.0, t_ground_y() - 10.0,
                          t_combi_w() + 12.0, 12.0, 240, 70, 90, 230);
        bussin;
    }

    🚽 Materialised: pick the frame from the sub-state. Wind holds the raised
    🚽 bat; the swing sweeps it down; recovery rests low (and is the opening).
    rizz fi = 4;
    edgy (state == t_cs_swing()) {
        chad prog = clampf(anim / t_combi_swing_t(), 0.0, 1.0);
        fi = 4.0 - prog * 4.0;
    }
    edgy (state == t_cs_recover()) { fi = 0; }

    edgy (tex >= 0) {
        🚽 Faces RIGHT natively, so facing left (dir < 0) mirrors -- negative
        🚽 source width, anchor to (fw - anchor). Same path as U Din Din.
        chad fw  = t_combi_frame_w();
        chad fh  = t_combi_frame_h();
        chad anc = t_combi_anchor();
        chad col = fi * fw;
        chad srcw = fw;
        edgy (dir < 0) {
            srcw = 0.0 - fw;
            anc  = fw - anc;
        }
        rl_draw_texture_rec(tex, col, 0.0, srcw, fh,
                            x + w / 2.0 - anc, y + h - fh,
                            255, 255, 255, 255);
    }
    amogus {
        🚽 Fallback: a tall dark figure with a raised bat, so the fight is
        🚽 playable with no atlas (same tex >= 0 rule as every other boss).
        rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, h, 40, 40, 52, 255);
        rl_draw_rectangle(x + w * 0.3, y + 12.0, 12.0, 12.0, 250, 250, 250, 255);
        rl_draw_rectangle(x + w * 0.32, y + 15.0, 6.0, 6.0, 20, 20, 20, 255);
        chad bx = x + w;
        edgy (dir < 0) { bx = x - 44.0; }
        rl_draw_rectangle(bx, y + 24.0, 44.0, 10.0, 150, 110, 60, 255);
    }
}

skibidi draw_boss(chad x, chad y, rizz kind, rizz phase, chad anim, rizz dir,
                  rizz state, chad dest_x, rizz script_i,
                  rizz tex_shark, rizz tex_croc, rizz tex_dindin,
                  rizz tex_combi) {
    chad w = boss_w(kind);
    chad h = boss_h(kind);

    edgy (kind == t_boss_combinasion()) {
        draw_combinasion(x, y, w, h, state, dir, dest_x, anim, tex_combi);
        bussin;
    }

    rizz tex = tex_croc;
    edgy (kind == t_boss_tralalero()) { tex = tex_shark; }
    edgy (kind == t_boss_dimdim()) { tex = tex_dindin; }

    edgy (tex >= 0) {
      edgy (kind == t_boss_dimdim()) {
        🚽 U Din Din: a 6-frame run cycle, always bottom-aligned (he's on the
        🚽 ground). The art faces LEFT, so charging right (dir > 0) draws it
        🚽 mirrored -- negative source width flips the frame, and the anchor
        🚽 column mirrors to (fw - anchor).
        chad fw  = t_dindin_frame_w();
        chad fh  = t_dindin_frame_h();
        chad anc = t_dindin_anchor();
        rizz fi  = anim * t_dindin_anim_rate();
        rizz frame = fi % t_dindin_frames();
        chad col = frame * fw;
        chad srcw = fw;
        🚽 The art faces RIGHT natively, so charging LEFT (dir < 0) draws it
        🚽 mirrored -- negative source width flips the frame, anchor mirrors to
        🚽 (fw - anchor). Charging right uses the frame as-is.
        edgy (dir < 0) {
            srcw = 0.0 - fw;
            anc  = fw - anc;
        }
        rl_draw_texture_rec(tex, col, 0.0, srcw, fh,
                            x + w / 2.0 - anc, y + h - fh,
                            255, 255, 255, 255);
      }
      amogus {
        🚽 Frame 1 is the opening in both atlases. That is the whole tell --
        🚽 jaws wide -- and the one second in three cycles where the bat
        🚽 connects.
        🚽
        🚽 Neither is mirrored, unlike Patapim. Tralalero chases from
        🚽 behind, so the art's own right-facing IS toward the player, and
        🚽 once he has leapt past, right-facing means his back is turned --
        🚽 which is exactly why he is open. Positive source width also means
        🚽 the anchor column maps straight through rather than to
        🚽 (fw - anchor), which a mirror would require.
        chad fw = t_shark_frame_w();
        chad fh = t_shark_frame_h();
        chad anc = t_shark_anchor();
        edgy (kind == t_boss_bombardiro()) {
            fw  = t_croc_frame_w();
            fh  = t_croc_frame_h();
            anc = t_croc_anchor();
        }
        chad col = 0.0;
        edgy (phase == t_boss_open()) { col = fw; }

        🚽 Tralalero stands on the ground, so his art is bottom-aligned to
        🚽 the box. Bombardiro flies and his frames are centre-aligned, so
        🚽 his box and frame share a centre instead.
        chad dy = y + h - fh;
        edgy (kind == t_boss_bombardiro()) { dy = y + (h - fh) / 2.0; }

        rl_draw_texture_rec(tex, col, 0.0, fw, fh,
                            x + w / 2.0 - anc, dy,
                            255, 255, 255, 255);
      }
    }
    amogus {
        edgy (kind == t_boss_tralalero()) {
            🚽 A shark on three shoes. Grey body, pale belly, one eye, and
            🚽 the legs that make him the joke.
            rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, h - 22.0, 96, 108, 120, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x, y + h * 0.45, w * 0.82, h * 0.30,
                              206, 210, 214, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + w * 0.55, y - 16.0, w * 0.18, 18.0,
                              96, 108, 120, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + 14.0, y + 18.0, 12.0, 12.0, 250, 250, 250, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + 16.0, y + 21.0, 6.0, 6.0, 20, 20, 20, 255);
            flex (rizz i = 0; i < 3; i = i + 1) {
                chad sx = x + 20.0 + i * 38.0;
                rl_draw_rectangle(sx, y + h - 22.0, 12.0, 16.0, 70, 60, 54, 255);
                rl_draw_rectangle(sx - 4.0, y + h - 8.0, 26.0, 10.0,
                                  240, 240, 240, 255);
            }
        }
        amogus edgy (kind == t_boss_dimdim()) {
            🚽 A blocky orange bruiser, for when the atlas is missing.
            rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, h * 0.42, 235, 120, 30, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x, y + h * 0.42, w, h * 0.58, 214, 92, 44, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + w * 0.5, y + 12.0, 12.0, 12.0,
                              250, 250, 250, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + w * 0.52, y + 15.0, 6.0, 6.0, 20, 20, 20, 255);
        }
        amogus {
            🚽 A crocodile with wings and a bomb bay.
            rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, h, 84, 124, 78, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x, y + h * 0.62, w * 0.9, h * 0.24,
                              196, 206, 170, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x - 26.0, y + 10.0, 30.0, 20.0, 84, 124, 78, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + w * 0.2, y - 14.0, w * 0.6, 14.0,
                              120, 120, 128, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + 12.0, y + 14.0, 12.0, 12.0, 250, 250, 250, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + 14.0, y + 17.0, 6.0, 6.0, 20, 20, 20, 255);
            flex (rizz i = 0; i < 5; i = i + 1) {
                rl_draw_rectangle(x + 10.0 + i * 20.0, y + h - 6.0, 10.0, 6.0,
                                  60, 50, 44, 255);
            }
        }
    }

    🚽 The opening ring, for a boss with no art yet.
    🚽
    🚽 It exists because a one-second window nobody can see is guesswork. A
    🚽 boss WITH art does not need it: the open frame is a different pose --
    🚽 Tralalero's jaws come wide open -- and he is on the other side of
    🚽 Tung by then, which is a second cue. Drawing it anyway would also
    🚽 look wrong, because the ring traces the 140x96 collision box while
    🚽 the art is 168px wide, so it would cut straight through his tail.
    edgy (tex < 0) {
        edgy (phase == t_boss_open()) {
            rl_draw_rectangle(x - 4.0, y - 4.0, w + 8.0, 4.0, 255, 214, 64, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x - 4.0, y + h, w + 8.0, 4.0, 255, 214, 64, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x - 4.0, y, 4.0, h, 255, 214, 64, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + w, y, 4.0, h, 255, 214, 64, 255);
        }
    }
}

🚽 The shell and the blast it becomes. Both sprites are drawn CENTRED on
🚽 their collision box rather than aligned to it: the blast's art is 77px of
🚽 spreading fire over a 64px box on purpose, so the outer flames are
🚽 decoration you can stand in, and centring is what makes that symmetric.
🚽 Where a falling bomb is going to hit, drawn on the ground line the moment
🚽 it is dropped.
🚽
🚽 This is the only warning the player gets. Without it they were tracking an
🚽 11px shell of rgb(34,34,40) against a rgb(12,14,34) sky while it crossed a
🚽 third of the screen in half a second -- see t_bomb_fall_time().
🚽
🚽 It tightens as impact approaches, so "how soon" is readable at a glance
🚽 without a number: a wide faint band is a bomb you have time for, a narrow
🚽 bright one is a bomb you do not.
skibidi draw_bomb_mark(chad lx, chad by, chad t_left) {
    chad frac = clampf(t_left / t_bomb_fall_time(), 0.0, 1.0);

    🚽 A guide line from the bomb straight down to where it will hit. Bombs
    🚽 fall straight (bomb_landing_x()), so this is exactly vertical and
    🚽 cannot mislead -- and it is what answers "where are they coming
    🚽 from", by tying each mark to the shell that made it.
    rl_draw_rectangle(lx - 1.0, by, 2.0, t_ground_y() - by, 255, 140, 60, 80);

    🚽 The mark sits ON the ground band, fully opaque.
    🚽
    🚽 It used to straddle the ground line at 35% alpha, which put half of it
    🚽 over the foliage layer and half over the ground -- a washed-out colour
    🚽 across a boundary between two different backgrounds. That is why it
    🚽 could not be read. Solid, below the line, one background.
    chad w = t_bomb_mark_w() * (0.40 + 0.60 * frac);
    chad h = t_bomb_mark_h();
    chad y = t_ground_y() + 3.0;
    rl_draw_rectangle(lx - w / 2.0, y, w, h, 18, 12, 8, 255);
    rl_draw_rectangle(lx - w / 2.0 + 2.0, y + 2.0, w - 4.0, h - 4.0,
                      255, 150, 50, 255);

    🚽 A bright core that widens as impact nears, so "how soon" reads at a
    🚽 glance without a number.
    chad cw = w * (1.0 - frac) * 0.7 + 5.0;
    rl_draw_rectangle(lx - cw / 2.0, y + 2.0, cw, h - 4.0, 255, 238, 160, 255);
}

skibidi draw_bomb(chad x, chad y, chad w, chad h, cap burning,
                  rizz tex_bomb, rizz tex_blast) {
    rizz tex = tex_bomb;
    chad fw  = t_bomb_frame_w();
    chad fh  = t_bomb_frame_h();
    edgy (burning) {
        tex = tex_blast;
        fw  = t_blast_frame_w();
        fh  = t_blast_frame_h();
    }

    edgy (tex >= 0) {
        rl_draw_texture_rec(tex, 0.0, 0.0, fw, fh,
                            x + (w - fw) / 2.0, y + (h - fh) / 2.0,
                            255, 255, 255, 255);
    }
    amogus {
        edgy (burning) {
            rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, h, 255, 148, 40, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + w * 0.15, y + h * 0.25, w * 0.7, h * 0.5,
                              255, 226, 120, 255);
        }
        amogus {
            rl_draw_rectangle(x, y, w, h, 34, 34, 40, 255);
            rl_draw_rectangle(x + w * 0.35, y - 6.0, w * 0.3, 6.0,
                              190, 140, 60, 255);
        }
    }
}

🚽 Three pips, one per bonk still owed. Drawn top-centre so it does not
🚽 fight the hearts (top-left) or the score (top-right).
skibidi draw_boss_bar(rizz kind, rizz bonks, cap ready) {
    chad bw = 64.0;
    chad x0 = t_screen_w() / 2.0 - (t_boss_bonks() * bw) / 2.0;
    rl_draw_rectangle(x0 - 8.0, 20.0, t_boss_bonks() * bw + 16.0, 26.0,
                      0, 0, 0, 140);
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < t_boss_bonks(); i = i + 1) {
        edgy (i < t_boss_bonks() - bonks) {
            rl_draw_rectangle(x0 + i * bw + 4.0, 24.0, bw - 8.0, 18.0,
                              214, 64, 64, 255);
        }
        amogus {
            rl_draw_rectangle(x0 + i * bw + 4.0, 24.0, bw - 8.0, 18.0,
                              60, 40, 40, 255);
        }
    }
    edgy (kind == t_boss_tralalero()) {
        rl_draw_text_int("TRALALERO TRALALA x", bonks, 0, x0 - 8.0, 50.0, 18,
                         255, 214, 64, 255);
    }
    amogus edgy (kind == t_boss_dimdim()) {
        rl_draw_text_int("U DIN DIN x", bonks, 0, x0 - 8.0, 50.0, 18,
                         255, 214, 64, 255);
    }
    amogus edgy (kind == t_boss_combinasion()) {
        rl_draw_text_int("LA GRANDE COMBINASION x", bonks, 0, x0 - 8.0, 50.0, 18,
                         255, 214, 64, 255);
    }
    amogus {
        rl_draw_text_int("BOMBARDIRO CROCODILO x", bonks, 0, x0 - 8.0, 50.0, 18,
                         255, 214, 64, 255);
    }

    🚽 The one thing the player has to act on, said out loud.
    🚽
    🚽 `ready` is "the boss has ARRIVED", not "the boss is in its open
    🚽 phase". Those differ by the 0.78s Tralalero spends leaping over
    🚽 Tung, and prompting during the leap would teach exactly the mistake
    🚽 that made the fight feel impossible: swing on sight, hit nothing,
    🚽 and spend the real window in t_attack_total()'s cooldown.
    edgy (ready) {
        rizz pw = rl_measure_text("TUNG HIM  --  X", 30);
        rl_draw_text("TUNG HIM  --  X", t_screen_w() / 2 - pw / 2, 78, 30,
                     255, 96, 96, 255);
    }
}
